  "summary": "Uppada Jamdani saree (or sari) is a  silk sari style woven in Uppada of Kakinada district in the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh.",
  "description": "Uppada Jamdani saree (or sari) is a  silk sari style woven in Uppada of Kakinada district in the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh. It was registered as one of the geographical indication from Andhra Pradesh by Geographical Indications of Goods (Registration and Protection) Act, 1999. Uppada Jamdani saris are known for their light weight.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Andhra Pradesh; registration 2008–09), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
